{"issue":{"title":"Add a jsonl-lint tool that reports every non-JSON row of a JSONL file by line number","problem":"The repo has no JSONL checker. `packages/` does not exist, the README says \"No tools yet: `packages/` is empty\", and the root `npm test` prints 'no workspaces under packages/' and passes. Nothing in the repo can be pointed at a JSONL journal to find torn or hand-edited rows. When one of those rows breaks a reader, the only way to find it is by hand.","reason":"Journals are kept as JSONL. One torn write (a half-written last row) or a bad hand edit makes every reader of the file fail. A small standalone checker that names each bad row by line number, and fails with a non-zero exit code, lets people and scripts catch this before a reader trips on it.","outcome":"After `npm ci` at the repo root there is a `jsonl-lint` command from a new zero-dependency workspace under `packages/`. Run on a file, it prints one line for each row that is not valid JSON, with that row's line number, and exits non-zero if there are any. It exits 0 on a clean file and gives an error with a non-zero exit when the file is missing. Its `node:test` suite runs under the root `npm test` and in CI.","expect":["A new npm workspace directory `packages/jsonl-lint/` exists, its package.json declares a `bin` named `jsonl-lint`, it has no `dependencies` entry (or an empty one), and `npm ci` at the repo root succeeds with the committed package-lock.json","After `npm ci`, running `./node_modules/.bin/jsonl-lint F` on a file F whose every row is valid JSON (rows `{\"a\":1}`, `[1,2]`, `\"s\"`, each ending in a newline) exits 0 and prints no line starting with `F:`","After `npm ci`, running `./node_modules/.bin/jsonl-lint F` on a file F with the rows `{\"a\":1}`, `{\"a\":`, `[1,2]`, `not json`, `{\"b\":2}` (newline-terminated) exits 1, its combined stdout+stderr has a line starting with `F:2:` and a line starting with `F:4:`, and no line starting with `F:1:`, `F:3:` or `F:5:`. F is the path exactly as passed, and line numbers are 1-based.","After `npm ci`, a torn last row with no trailing newline is reported: on a file F with the content `{\"a\":1}\\n{\"b` the command exits 1 and has a line starting with `F:2:`","After `npm ci`, an empty line in the middle of the file is reported as invalid: on a file F with the content `{\"a\":1}\\n\\n{\"b\":2}\\n` the command exits 1 and has a line starting with `F:2:`. A single trailing newline at the end of the file is not a row, so `{\"a\":1}\\n` exits 0.","After `npm ci`, an empty (0-byte) file exits 0","After `npm ci`, running `./node_modules/.bin/jsonl-lint /tmp/does-not-exist-jsonl-lint.jsonl` exits 2, writes a message containing that path to stderr, and prints no Node stack trace (no line starting with `    at `)","After `npm ci`, running `./node_modules/.bin/jsonl-lint` with no file argument exits 2 and writes a usage message to stderr","`packages/jsonl-lint` has a `node:test` suite that covers a clean file, a file with several invalid rows (asserting each line number), and a missing file. `npm test` at the repo root runs it and passes.","The CI `test` workflow passes on the pull request","README.md no longer says `packages/` is empty or that there are no tools. It lists `jsonl-lint` and shows how to run it."],"proofs":[{"line":"A new npm workspace directory `packages/jsonl-lint/` exists, its package.json declares a `bin` named `jsonl-lint`, it has no `dependencies` entry (or an empty one), and `npm ci` at the repo root succeeds with the committed package-lock.json","proof":"run","how":"npm ci && node -e 'const p=require(\"./packages/jsonl-lint/package.json\");const b=typeof p.bin===\"string\"?{[p.name]:p.bin}:p.bin;if(!b||!b[\"jsonl-lint\"])throw new Error(\"no jsonl-lint bin\");if(p.dependencies&&Object.keys(p.dependencies).length)throw new Error(\"has deps\");console.log(\"ok\")' && test -x node_modules/.bin/jsonl-lint"},{"line":"After `npm ci`, running `./node_modules/.bin/jsonl-lint F` on a file F whose every row is valid JSON (rows `{\"a\":1}`, `[1,2]`, `\"s\"`, each ending in a newline) exits 0 and prints no line starting with `F:`","proof":"run","how":"F=/tmp/jl-ok.jsonl; printf '{\"a\":1}\\n[1,2]\\n\"s\"\\n' > $F; ./node_modules/.bin/jsonl-lint $F > /tmp/jl-out 2>&1; echo exit=$?; ! grep -q \"^$F:\" /tmp/jl-out && echo no-reports  # expect exit=0 and no-reports"},{"line":"After `npm ci`, running `./node_modules/.bin/jsonl-lint F` on a file F with the rows `{\"a\":1}`, `{\"a\":`, `[1,2]`, `not json`, `{\"b\":2}` (newline-terminated) exits 1, its combined stdout+stderr has a line starting with `F:2:` and a line starting with `F:4:`, and no line starting with `F:1:`, `F:3:` or `F:5:`. F is the path exactly as passed, and line numbers are 1-based.","proof":"run","how":"F=/tmp/jl-bad.jsonl; printf '{\"a\":1}\\n{\"a\":\\n[1,2]\\nnot json\\n{\"b\":2}\\n' > $F; ./node_modules/.bin/jsonl-lint $F > /tmp/jl-out 2>&1; echo exit=$?; grep -c \"^$F:[24]:\" /tmp/jl-out; grep -c \"^$F:[135]:\" /tmp/jl-out  # expect exit=1, then 2, then 0"},{"line":"After `npm ci`, a torn last row with no trailing newline is reported: on a file F with the content `{\"a\":1}\\n{\"b` the command exits 1 and has a line starting with `F:2:`","proof":"run","how":"F=/tmp/jl-torn.jsonl; printf '{\"a\":1}\\n{\"b' > $F; ./node_modules/.bin/jsonl-lint $F > /tmp/jl-out 2>&1; echo exit=$?; grep -c \"^$F:2:\" /tmp/jl-out  # expect exit=1 and 1"},{"line":"After `npm ci`, an empty line in the middle of the file is reported as invalid: on a file F with the content `{\"a\":1}\\n\\n{\"b\":2}\\n` the command exits 1 and has a line starting with `F:2:`. A single trailing newline at the end of the file is not a row, so `{\"a\":1}\\n` exits 0.","proof":"run","how":"F=/tmp/jl-blank.jsonl; printf '{\"a\":1}\\n\\n{\"b\":2}\\n' > $F; ./node_modules/.bin/jsonl-lint $F > /tmp/jl-out 2>&1; echo exit=$?; grep -c \"^$F:2:\" /tmp/jl-out; G=/tmp/jl-one.jsonl; printf '{\"a\":1}\\n' > $G; ./node_modules/.bin/jsonl-lint $G; echo exit=$?  # expect exit=1, 1, then exit=0"},{"line":"After `npm ci`, an empty (0-byte) file exits 0","proof":"run","how":"F=/tmp/jl-empty.jsonl; : > $F; ./node_modules/.bin/jsonl-lint $F; echo exit=$?  # expect exit=0"},{"line":"After `npm ci`, running `./node_modules/.bin/jsonl-lint /tmp/does-not-exist-jsonl-lint.jsonl` exits 2, writes a message containing that path to stderr, and prints no Node stack trace (no line starting with `    at `)","proof":"run","how":"rm -f /tmp/does-not-exist-jsonl-lint.jsonl; ./node_modules/.bin/jsonl-lint /tmp/does-not-exist-jsonl-lint.jsonl 2>/tmp/jl-err >/tmp/jl-stdout; echo exit=$?; grep -c '/tmp/does-not-exist-jsonl-lint.jsonl' /tmp/jl-err; cat /tmp/jl-err /tmp/jl-stdout | grep -c '^    at '  # expect exit=2, >=1, 0"},{"line":"After `npm ci`, running `./node_modules/.bin/jsonl-lint` with no file argument exits 2 and writes a usage message to stderr","proof":"run","how":"./node_modules/.bin/jsonl-lint 2>/tmp/jl-err </dev/null; echo exit=$?; test -s /tmp/jl-err && cat /tmp/jl-err  # expect exit=2 and a non-empty usage message"},{"line":"`packages/jsonl-lint` has a `node:test` suite that covers a clean file, a file with several invalid rows (asserting each line number), and a missing file. `npm test` at the repo root runs it and passes.","proof":"run","how":"npm ci && npm test 2>&1 | tee /tmp/jl-test; echo exit=${PIPESTATUS[0]}; then read the test files under packages/jsonl-lint to confirm they import from 'node:test' and cover the clean, multi-invalid-row (line numbers asserted) and missing-file cases. Expect exit=0, with jsonl-lint tests in the output."},{"line":"The CI `test` workflow passes on the pull request","proof":"ci","how":"The `test` check from .github/workflows/test.yml (npm ci, npm test) on the PR head is green"},{"line":"README.md no longer says `packages/` is empty or that there are no tools. It lists `jsonl-lint` and shows how to run it.","proof":"read","how":"Read README.md at the PR head: the 'No tools yet' bullet is gone or rewritten, and jsonl-lint is listed with an example invocation"}],"non_goals":["Schema validation or checking row shapes or fields: only 'is this row valid JSON'","Repairing, rewriting or truncating the file","Reading from stdin, checking several files in one run, or globbing directories","Publishing the package to npm or any release step","Changes to the harness in suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine or to the journal readers themselves","Streaming or performance tuning for very large files beyond reading an ordinary journal"],"assumptions":["The tool goes in a new workspace `packages/jsonl-lint` with a bin named `jsonl-lint`, following the repo's one-folder-per-tool layout. The request only says 'a small jsonl-lint tool'.","A row is valid if JSON.parse accepts it as any JSON value (object, array, string, number, boolean, null), not only objects","Rows are split on '\\n'. A trailing '\\r' (CRLF) is JSON whitespace and does not by itself make a row invalid.","A single trailing newline at the end of the file does not make an extra row. An empty or whitespace-only line anywhere else is reported as invalid, because strict JSONL has no blank rows. A 0-byte file is valid.","Each bad row is reported as one line starting with `<path as passed>:<1-based line>:` followed by a short reason (the `file:line:` convention). Whether that goes to stdout or stderr is left to the builder, and the checks read both.","Exit codes: 0 when clean, 1 when any row is invalid, 2 for a missing or unreadable file or a missing argument. That way a script can tell 'bad rows' apart from 'could not check'.","The tool keeps going after the first bad row and reports every one, because the request says 'every row'"]}}